<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Cashbuild first half flat, upbeat on future.</title>
<headline>Cashbuild first half flat, upbeat on future.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>26 weeks to Dec 28 vs 27 weeks to Dec 30, 1995</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     15.5	  vs 15.3</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  -	    vs  -</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   3.60	  vs 3.56</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   6.83	  vs 6.28</p>
<p>    Tax			 2.56	  vs 2.47</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   2.84	  vs 1.59</p>
<p>    Operating income	9.67	  vs 7.86</p>
<p>    Turnover		  401.47	vs 361.50</p>
<p>Full name: Cashbuild Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said early results of repositioning of the business from that of a rural cash and carry wholesaler to that of an urban-based mass discounter were very encouraging.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
